  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1105 PM CST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\nTuesday and Wednesday are shaping up to be drier days as there will \nbe a lack of moisture feed into the southern plains. This doesn't \nmean the weather will be quiet as a weather system ejects out of the \ndesert southwest. Without moisture this system will not be able to \nproduce rain, instead it will lead to windy conditions across the \npanhandles. The current trajectory of this system favors the \nnorthern panhandles for seeing the strongest winds. The winds will \nbe mainly southerly which will allow for warmer air to stream back \nacross the region leading to warmer, if still mild temperatures. \n\nThursday into the weekend will likely see another weather system \nmove eastward from the desert southwest across the southern plains. \nThis slower moving weather system has a low to medium chance of \nbeing able to source moisture and move that across the panhandles. \nIf this occurs then the panhandles can see another period of active \nweather from rain showers and thunderstorms. This system is unlikely \nto bring much in the way of colder air so temperatures will still \nmore likely than not remain mild.",
